alid supported successor shape (the parser prescribes `planmode = \"dual\"` for deeper review rather than `safety_class = \"adjudication\"`), then verify the complete block parses and mints both successors -> @owner\nVERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=1\n=============== docs/reviews/wi-586-adjudicate-llr-207-llr-208/003-ADJUDICATE-9c563df.md\n- [RETURN] LLR-207 -> define the one tree-bound, logged-session verdict record shared by the merge gate and review scheduler -> SR-156 requires a fail-closed serial verdict seam and TC-205 is the right child, but two Detail clauses contradict the implemented branch-tip/read-only-walk contracts and the multi-log, trailer-carrier, and reset-peel clauses remain unverified -> not ready\n- [RETURN] TC-205 -> verify both verdict-record readers and every fail-closed opposite claimed by LLR-207 on the same governing identity -> the SR-156/LLR-207/IF-175 chain is correctly targeted, but the cited evidence still omits the multi-log ambiguity, trailer-carrier mismatch, and reset-peel/refusal arms and its Method still misstates the docs/work identity assertion -> not ready\n- [RETURN] LLR-208 -> make the per-review-scope rollup derived trunk-owned state, regenerated and freshness-gated at the serial seam while standing down on work branches -> SR-170 calls for that exclusive-writer design and TC-206 covers generation, freshness, and stand-down, but no cited test pins the claimed trunk_step regeneration wiring -> not ready\n- [RETURN] TC-206 -> verify rollup generation, all freshness answers and remedies, collision refusal, trunk regeneration, and work-branch stand-down -> its evidence covers every stated arm except that the serial trunk step actually carries and runs the verdict-rollup regenerator, so the Expected claim can become false while all cited tests stay green -> not ready\nOUTCOME: RETURN rows=4\n=============== docs/reviews/wi-586-adjudicate-llr-207-llr-208/004-REVIEW-A-3c7764c.md\n# REVIEW-A — WI-586 adjudicate LLR-207/LLR-208