e earlier\n  findings — re-drive them (mutation-test any \"no test covers X\" claim; a\n  guard whose deletion leaves the suite green is a confirmed gap). It DOES\n  mean the useful next act is the merge that mints the drafts, not a further\n  reread; say so in the verdict as an observation for the coordinator.\n- Check for an outstanding CHANGES-REQUESTED against the *dispositions* and\n  apply it — that rework is the session's real deliverable on a repeat round,\n  and it is what unblocks the mint. Verify with\n  `intake.parse_dispositions(text, path)` → `refusal=None` and the expected\n  draft count.\n- `bar` on a disposition draft must match the deliverable: new pytest\n  regressions are `DevStg-Tests` (14 steps), not `DevStg-Reqs` (12) — the\n  extra two are `design-flows` and `trajectory` (`kitlib/ladder.py:79`).\n- pytest lives in the TRUNK venv, not the lane:\n  `/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template/.venv/bin/python`. The commit hook\n  runs `/usr/local/bin/python3`, so the `format`/ruff step SKIPs loudly —\n  environment, not a regression (see [[ruff-0-16-skew-scaffold-lint-failures]]).\n\nRelated: [[loop-review-runaway-2026-09-03]],\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]], [[verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
