ing detects. Its other clauses genuinely bind (I read `gen_verdict_rollup.py` in full).\n\n**The design is not returned.** Findings 1–2 are wording that contradicts the module, not a mechanism to reopen.\n\n## Also applied: the outstanding rework\n\nRound 004's CHANGES-REQUESTED had sat unaddressed. All three fixed, each verified first — notably the MAJOR: I confirmed `DevStg-Reqs` = 12 steps vs `DevStg-Tests` = 14 (adding `design-flows`, `trajectory`) and that `ladder.py:79` defines the latter as \"the test set for those obligations in work\". Both drafts now declare `DevStg-Tests` and re-parse with `refusal=None`, 2 drafts.\n\n`check.py --jobs 0` → **RESULT: PASS**. No `Status` byte, registry cell, or `docs/archive/last_approved/` entry moved; `intake.py snapshot` was not run in any form, so the `WI-584` blocker round 001 hit is not reached by this act.\n\n## One thing worth your attention\n\nThese rows have now been read three times against unchanged text, because an adjudicator may flip a `Status` but may never edit the cells its findings name — the repair can only travel through the disposition drafts at merge. **A RETURN verdict structurally cannot change the next reread.** The drafts are now correct and parse, so the next useful act is the merge that mints them, not a fourth reread. I recorded this in the verdict as an observation for the coordinator rather than acting on it, since it falsifies no cell in the batch — but if the loop re-arms this lane, that's the loop spending an hour to re-derive an answer it already has."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":408,"cache_read_input_tokens":116842,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":408},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3aa25326-d0fa-4e17-bf43-3979ded3d7c7","uuid":